Let \( S \) be the set of all integers \( n \) such that \( 1 \leq n \leq 100 \). For each \( n \in S \), define the function \( f(n) \) as follows:

\[ f(n) = \begin{cases} 
n + 5 & \text{if } n \text{ is odd} \\
n - 7 & \text{if } n \text{ is even}
\end{cases} \]

Define the sequence \( (a_k) \) by \( a_1 = 1 \) and \( a_{k+1} = f(a_k) \) for \( k \geq 1 \). Find the number of distinct elements in the set \( \{a_1, a_2, a_3, \ldots, a_{100}\} \).

Find the dimension of the sum of the image subspaces of the following matrices:
[
\begin{pmatrix}
1 & 2 \\
3 & 4
\end{pmatrix}
\quad
\begin{pmatrix}
2 & 0 \\
2 & 3
\end{pmatrix}
\quad
\begin{pmatrix}
1 & 0 \\
0 & 0
\end{pmatrix}
]
\[
\text{dim}(\text{im}(A_1)) + \text{dim}(\text{im}(A_2)) - \text{dim}(\text{im}(A_3))
\]

Let \( f(n) \) be a function defined for all positive integers \( n \) such that:
\[ f(n) = \begin{cases} 
n + 1 & \text{if } n \text{ is odd} \\
\frac{n}{2} & \text{if } n \text{ is even}
\end{cases} \]
Define a sequence \( a_1, a_2, a_3, \ldots \) where \( a_1 = 2023 \) and \( a_{k+1} = f(a_k) \) for \( k \geq 1 \). Find the smallest positive integer \( m \) such that \( a_m = 1 \).

Let \( f: \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{N} \) be a function defined such that \( f(1) = 1 \) and for all \( n \geq 1 \),
\[ f(n+1) = \begin{cases} 
f(n) + 2 & \text{if } n \text{ is odd} \\
f(n) \div 2 & \text{if } n \text{ is even} 
\end{cases} \]
Find the smallest positive integer \( k \) such that \( f(k) = 1 \).
